      "pins": ["C6.1", "C6.2"],
      "nets": ["PWM1_C2", "PWM1"],
      "observed": "In the top-right PWM selector area, the row between PWM1_C2 and PWM1 contains a capacitor labeled C6 with value 100u. The visible jumper references are R9, C6, R11, and R12; no R10 0 Ω jumper is present in the position implied by the schematic note.",
      "expected": "R10 should be a 0 Ω jumper selecting PWM1_C2 for Core2/CoreS3, as specified for R9–R12. A 100 µF capacitor is not an appropriate component in this PWM signal-selection path.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet /, top-right: \"C6 100u\""},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet /, top-right: \"Short R10, R10 for Core2 and CoreS3 / Short R9, R11 for others\""},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R9–R12 | 0 Ω (jumpers) | Select which M5Stack bus pin (pin 19/21 for ch.1, pin 20/22 for ch.2) supplies PWM1/PWM2"}
      ],
      "impact": "For a Core2/CoreS3 PWM-mode build that should short R10, the PWM1_C2-to-PWM1 path is AC-coupled or blocked by a 100 µF capacitor instead of being a low-resistance jumper. The PWM servo signal for channel 1 would be heavily distorted or absent, and the M5Stack GPIO would see an unintended large capacitive load.",
      "confidence": 0.78
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic shows a 100 µF capacitor C6 in the PWM1_C2 jumper position where the design requires a 0 Ω R10 jumper, which would break or distort PWM servo operation for the Core2/CoreS3 selection mode."
}

